SUSPECTED BUG: Save returns errors.Join(werr, flush(f), f.Close()). In the default
build flush always returns nil, but Join drops nil operands and still returns the
others. Expected: the os.Create origin under "source: create: %w" AND, under an
errors.Join link, the (*os.File).Write origins (seal_write_call_site) and the
(*os.File).Close origins (close_in_deferred_closure). Actual: only the os.Create entry;
the whole Join disappears as soon as one operand is a call that can only return nil
(a literal nil operand is handled correctly). Cause: when a callee summary is
substituted, the operand sets are multiplied and an empty set gives an empty product
(internal/summary/eval.go, mapTreeRaw). Compare save_join_durable, where flush can fail.
-- args --
source/source.go:@save
